<%# /site-chat (Legal L76 S8): "Run by 127" in a member's site chat links here. What 127 does for the business, pointing to Privacy 7C. %>
<main class="wrap" style="padding:120px 24px;max-width:720px">
  <div class="eyebrow">Site chat</div>
  <h1 class="display" style="font-size:44px;margin:14px 0">A chat run by 127, for the business you're visiting.</h1>
  <p class="muted">The chat on this business's website is an AI assistant. 127 runs it for the business as their service provider. Here's what that means for you.</p>
  <ul class="muted" style="line-height:1.7">
    <li>It answers only from the info the business marked public, and it can get things wrong. Check anything important with the business.</li>
    <li>Your chat is saved for the business, with the page you wrote from and any details you choose to leave so they can reply. They decide what the chat says and what happens next.</li>
    <li>It can't book, sell or take payment. Please don't share card numbers or health details in it.</li>
    <li>127 sends your messages to Anthropic only to write the answers. We don't use your chat for anything else or combine it with other businesses' information.</li>
    <li>The business keeps each chat for 180 days after its last message, and can delete it sooner.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">Questions about your chat, or want it deleted? Ask the business. If you write to us, we'll pass your request on. More in our <a href="/privacy#7c-your-brain-ask-127-ai-team-site-chat-and-studio">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</main>
